    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n37488" root="لبد" body-key="l">
    
      <b><span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">نَاقَةٌ لَبِدَةٌ</span></b>  <i>A she-camel choked by eating much
of the plant called</i> <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">صِلِّيَان</span>: pl. <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">لَبَادَى</span>: [see <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">لَبِدَ</span>:]
(S:) or <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">إِبِلٌ لَبِدَةٌ</span>, and <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">لَبَادَى</span>, <i>camels having a
complaint of the belly from eating of the</i> <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">قَتَاد</span> [or
<i>tragacantha</i>]: and in like manner you say <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">ناقة</span>
<span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">لَبِدَةٌ</span>. (AHn, L.)

